<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Allen Stanford</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Robert Allen Stanford</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Allen Stanford is an American financier who built a banking and investment empire based in Antigua, where he became the largest private employer and was knighted in 2006. In 2009 US authorities charged him with running a Ponzi scheme worth about 7 billion dollars through his Stanford International Bank. He was convicted in 2012 and sentenced to 110 years in prison, and Antigua stripped him of his knighthood.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/allen-stanford.jpg" alt="Allen Stanford" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Marshals Service · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Allen_Stanford_mug_shot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
